# Cursor rules – Leadership Compass

You are working on a React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind single-page app with a Supabase (Postgres + Deno edge
functions) back end. See CLAUDE.md, docs/spec.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.

## Code style
- TypeScript strict; no `any` (use `unknown` and narrow). Functional React components with hooks.
- Imports use the `@/` alias. Keep feature code in `src/features/<feature>/`.
- Styling with Tailwind design tokens and the shared classes (btn-primary, btn-secondary, field-input, eyebrow).
- User-facing text: plain, friendly English; explain what happens and what to do next.

## Security and privacy
- Never hardcode keys, tokens or passwords. Secrets live in Supabase function secrets.
- Every new table: enable RLS, revoke defaults, add explicit policies. Privileged writes only via SECURITY DEFINER
  functions (`SET search_path = ''`) or edge functions using the service role after checking the caller.
- Do not log or send personal data to third parties. AI calls must go through `ai-insights` with names scrubbed.
- Keep the audit trail append-only; write audit rows for data-changing actions.

## Database
- Never edit an applied migration; add a new timestamped file in supabase/migrations.

## Quality
- Before finishing: `npm run lint`, `npx tsc -b`, `npm test`, `npm run build` must pass; Deno check for edge functions.
- Add unit tests (Vitest) for new pure logic.
- Pin new dependencies to exact versions at least two weeks old.
